<PageTitle>Information for law enforcement — Swoovr</PageTitle>
<div class="column">
    <div class="page-heading" data-law-enforcement-page>
        <h1>Information for law enforcement</h1>
        <p>How police, law-enforcement bodies and other authorities can contact Swoovr about member information or preserving records.</p>
    </div>
    <section class="card account-section">
        <h2>If someone is in immediate danger</h2>
        <p>Call <a href="tel:000">000</a>. Swoovr is not an emergency service.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card account-section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Send requests to <a href="mailto:lawenforcement@swoovr.app" data-authority-contact>lawenforcement@swoovr.app</a>. This is the only channel for authorities; we don't act on requests made through other email addresses, social media, direct messages or calls to individual staff.</p>
        <p>We don't publish a response-time commitment. We prioritise requests involving a threat to life or serious harm, and tell you when we have received yours.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card account-section">
        <h2>What to include</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Your agency, name, rank or role, and a contact number we can verify through your agency's official switchboard or directory.</li>
            <li>Your case reference and the formal request or legal instrument relied on (for example a warrant, court order, subpoena or statutory notice).</li>
            <li>Exactly what you're asking for, about whom, and for which period.</li>
            <li>Any deadline, and why if it's urgent.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="card account-section">
        <h2>How we handle requests</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>We verify every request independently before acting on it. A government email address alone is not enough.</li>
            <li>Preserving records and disclosing them are separate decisions. A request to preserve doesn't mean we will disclose.</li>
            <li>We disclose only what the law requires or permits, as narrowly as possible, and we may ask you to clarify or narrow a request.</li>
            <li>We may tell affected members about a request unless the law prohibits it or it would put someone at risk or prejudice an investigation.</li>
            <li>Requests from outside Australia generally need to come through mutual legal assistance or another channel recognised in Australia.</li>
            <li>Some information is held by our providers (for example identity verification). We'll tell you if a request needs to go to them.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <p class="help">Swoovr is operated by RePass Cloud Pty Ltd. Members can read about this in our <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.</p>
</div>
